<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Werner Report</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1970</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Werner Report was a plan for economic and monetary union in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-communities">European Communities</a>, presented in October 1970 by a group chaired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-werner">Pierre Werner</a>, prime minister of Luxembourg. It proposed reaching full union in stages within ten years, with fixed exchange rates, free movement of capital and coordinated economic policy. The currency turmoil of the 1970s halted it, but its ideas shaped the later path to the euro.</p></div>
